      <item>
        <title>GenAtlas: AI-designed heterogeneous catalysts at 1000x the discovery rate</title>
        <link>https://nature.com/natcatal</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://nature.com/natcatal</guid>
        <pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>Nature Catalysis</source>
        <description>GenAtlas is a graph-attention-based foundation model trained on 4.8M known catalytic reactions (OPCF, USPTO, Reaxys) + 12M DFT-computed surface energies. It designs heterogeneous catalysts (supported metal nanoparticles) with target activity + selectivity for C-H activation, CO2 reduction, and ammonia synthesis. On 23 industrial targets (BASF process roadmap), GenAtlas proposes 47 catalyst candidates per target, of which 31% show &gt; 2x activity vs the incumbent catalyst in high-throughput microreactor testing. The model also predicts catalyst lifetime (TOS to 50% deactivation) within ±25%. The paper releases a 47-candidate library across 23 targets, plus the GenAtlas-Inorganic dataset (12M DFT-computed surface energies for binary + ternary metal oxides).</description>
        <category>Chemistry - AI catalyst design</category>
        <dc:creator>GenAtlas Consortium (DeepMind + BASF + MIT)</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Holographic microscopy reconstruction via physics-informed diffusion</title>
        <link>https://nature.com/nmeth</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://nature.com/nmeth</guid>
        <pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>Nature Methods</source>
        <description>A physics-informed diffusion model reconstructs 3D microscopy volumes from 2D holograms (label-free, fast, low-phototoxic). The model embeds the wave equation as a differentiable forward operator, enabling unsupervised training on raw holograms without paired ground-truth volumes. On 4 modalities (DIC, phase-contrast, holographic, light-field), the model achieves SSIM 0.87-0.94 vs ground-truth confocal volumes, with 100x lower phototoxicity (no scanning required). Released as HoloScope-AI on PyPI + as a napari plugin. The pretrained models cover 9 cell lines (HeLa, HEK293, U2OS, organoids, neurons) and 5 imaging modalities.</description>
        <category>Biology - AI microscopy</category>
        <dc:creator>HHMI Janelia + Princeton</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>TabPFN v2: in-context tabular foundation model beats XGBoost on small data</title>
        <link>https://nature.com/articles/s41586-2026-04853-x</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://nature.com/articles/s41586-2026-04853-x</guid>
        <pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>Nature</source>
        <description>TabPFN v2 is a 100M-parameter foundation model for tabular classification + regression. At inference, it learns a new tabular task IN-CONTEXT from the training rows (no fine-tuning). On 458 small-data benchmarks (≤ 10k rows), TabPFN v2 beats XGBoost, CatBoost, and LightGBM by 5-12% accuracy. Key innovation: a Set-Transformer architecture with a &#x27;dynamic programming&#x27; attention mechanism that runs in O(n²) for n=10k rows (vs O(n³) for vanilla attention), enabling in-context learning at scale. Released as PyPI `tabpfn` v2 + on HuggingFace. The model is licensed Apache-2.0; runs on a single CPU at 2-5 sec per inference for n=1000.</description>
        <category>CS - Tabular foundation models</category>
        <dc:creator>Hollmann et al. (Google + TU Munich)</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>BioNeMo-2: 4B-param drug discovery foundation model + GenerativeProtein service</title>
        <link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/bionemo-2</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/bionemo-2</guid>
        <pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>NVIDIA blog</source>
        <description>BioNeMo-2 (4B params) is NVIDIA&#x27;s foundation model for drug discovery, trained on 2.1B protein sequences + 600M structures + 90M ligand-binding pairs. Released at GTC 2026 alongside the GenerativeProtein service (de novo protein binder design) + DockingFuser (binding pose refinement). On the CASP15 + CASP16 benchmarks, BioNeMo-2 achieves 0.85 GDT_TS for structure prediction (vs AlphaFold-Multimer&#x27;s 0.79) and 0.92 Top-1 for ligand-binding prediction (vs ChemNet&#x27;s 0.74). Available via NIM containers + NGC catalog. Free for academic research. Includes a 1000-GPU cloud credit for academic discovery teams.</description>
        <category>Biology - Drug discovery FM</category>
        <dc:creator>NVIDIA BioNeMo team</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>AMIE diagnostic LLM update: 85% diagnostic accuracy on NEJM CPC</title>
        <link>https://nature.com/nm</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://nature.com/nm</guid>
        <pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>Nature Medicine</source>
        <description>AMIE (Articulate Medical Intelligence Explorer) is updated with a 70B-parameter multimodal model (text + lab values + chest X-ray + ECG). Achieves 85% top-1 diagnostic accuracy on the 200-case NEJM Clinicopathological Conference (CPC) benchmark — surpassing primary-care physicians (76%) and matching specialist experts (87%). AMIE also includes a &#x27;diagnostic reasoning chain&#x27; output: it lists the differential diagnosis with probabilities + evidence + next-step workup. The reasoning chain is independently evaluated by blinded physicians as &#x27;clinically useful&#x27; in 91% of cases. Pilot deployment in 3 NHS trusts (GP-to-specialist referral triage) shows 23% reduction in unnecessary referrals + 18% improvement in correct-1st-specialist-seen rate.</description>
        <category>CS - Medical LLM</category>
        <dc:creator>Google Research (DeepMind Health)</dc:creator>
      </item>
